{
  "_comment": [
    "Observed GPU memory peaks per family, extracted from returned job archives by",
    "scripts/measure_vram_bounds.py. NOT part of the evaluator closure -- deliberately",
    "not in families.json, which is a CONFIG_MEMBER whose modification would",
    "invalidate every attestation.",
    "A row is an OBSERVED PEAK of one past configuration. It is evidence toward an",
    "upper bound, never the bound itself, and it must not be scaled to another",
    "configuration -- see notes/production-host/10-resource-upper-bound-rule.md.",
    "",
    "[Claude 2026-09-16] This file is a per-family MAXIMUM over the union of every cell ever",
    "measured, and it must only ever be updated that way. Running measure_vram_bounds.py --write",
    "over a subset of directories REPLACES it: doing that today cut 50 cells to 9 and LOWERED",
    "ppg from 7146 to 2418 MiB and rlvigen from 4549 to 1475, because the higher earlier",
    "observations were simply absent from the directories passed in. A bound that silently falls",
    "is the one failure this file exists to prevent -- it is read to decide whether a cell fits",
    "beside someone else's job, and the owner's rule is NEVER OOM, including other people's jobs.",
    "Caught by a peer session diffing the working copy against HEAD, not by me.",
    "",
    "[Claude 2026-09-16, second correction the same day] ibac_sni's entry is REMOVED, not revised.",
    "It briefly read 22675 MiB. That figure was the sum of every compute process on a SHARED",
    "card: 21,300 MiB of it was a colleague's two processes at 10,650 each. measure_vram_bounds.py",
    "summed all compute processes while its own docstring claimed it filtered to our process tree;",
    "no such filter existed, and it cannot be added, because the cell's pids are container-namespace",
    "and gpu_compute_processes carries host pids. The script now names the field all_procs_peak_mib,",
    "flags shared_card and steady_state, and REFUSES to record a family peak from a row that is",
    "either. Caught by a peer session reading the pids, not by the instrument.",
    "",
    "ibac_sni is listed as WITHOUT a measurement rather than carried at a smaller number, because",
    "both available numbers are wrong in opposite directions. The 2,199 MiB from the 3-process cell",
    "UNDER-counts: that same cell's card_delta is 6,804 MiB, and the ~4.6 GiB gap is EGL render",
    "contexts, which are not compute apps and so never appear in a per-process sum. At procs=16 with",
    "one EGL context per worker that gap is the dominant term. The only figure the data supports is",
    "a LOWER bound of ~6.6 GiB, taken as the card delta at the moment the floor stood the cell down",
    "42.4 s in, while its process count was still climbing 2 -> 20.",
    "",
    "A real bound needs a cell that is not stood down in its first minute. One is running now on a",
    "near-exclusive card 1 under self-vram-cap.sh at 22,000 MiB; card_delta on that run is the",
    "measurement, because it is the only attribution that includes EGL."
  ],
